IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, sections 108 to 111 -- CEASING TO HOLD
-- OFFICE, REMOVAL OF DIRECTORS, A DIRECTOR'S RIGHT TO NOTICE AND TO BE HEARD, AND FILLING A VACANCY. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs. A fact that another module
-- of this piece works out (disqualification under s 105(1); the votes in s 107(g)) is a plain input and the
-- comment names the rule that works it out. A cross-reference to another piece is a plain input and says so.

§ `s 108 Ceasing to hold office`

§§ `s 108(2) Effective date of resignation`

-- Day granularity (fork F-P10-8): the text says "time"; this encoding counts in days.
-- src:1301 | Effective date of resignation
-- src:1302 | (2) A resignation of a director becomes effective at the time a written resignation is sent to the corporation, or at the time specified in the resignation, whichever is later.
@ref CBCA s 108(2) (src:1301-1302)
GIVEN `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date a resignation becomes effective within s 108(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation`
    WHEN JUST s THEN (IF s GREATER THAN `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation`
                      THEN s
                      ELSE `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation`)

-- src:1301 | Effective date of resignation
-- src:1302 | (2) A resignation of a director becomes effective at the time a written resignation is sent to the corporation, or at the time specified in the resignation, whichever is later.
@ref CBCA s 108(2) (src:1301-1302)
GIVEN `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the resignation has become effective on the day asked about within s 108(2)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST (`the date a resignation becomes effective within s 108(2)`
                                        `the date a written resignation is sent to the corporation`
                                        `the date specified in the resignation, if one is specified`)

§ `s 109 Removal of directors`

§§ `s 109(1) Removal of directors`

-- "Subject to paragraph 107(g)": where the articles provide for cumulative voting, the votes cast must meet the
-- threshold that paragraph sets (`the vote needed to remove the director is met within s 107(g)`, in
-- cb2-part10-election).
-- src:1303 | Removal of directors
-- src:1304 | 109 (1) Subject to paragraph 107(g), the shareholders of a corporation may by ordinary resolution at a special meeting remove any director or directors from office.
@ref CBCA s 109(1) (src:1303-1304)
GIVEN `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders may remove the director within s 109(1)` MEANS
        `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`
    AND `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders`
    AND (   NOT `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
         OR `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)`)

§§ `s 109(2) Exception`

-- src:1305 | Exception
-- src:1306 | (2) Where the holders of any class or series of shares of a corporation have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors, a director so elected may only be removed by an ordinary resolution at a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series.
@ref CBCA s 109(2) (src:1305-1306)
GIVEN `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a director elected by a class or series may be removed within s 109(2)` MEANS
        `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect`
    AND `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`
    AND `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series`
    AND (   NOT `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
         OR `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)`)

-- The two together: a class-elected director only by the class meeting (the special-meeting requirement of (1)
-- is read as displaced by the exception: fork F-P10-5); any other director under (1).
-- src:1303 | Removal of directors
-- src:1304 | 109 (1) Subject to paragraph 107(g), the shareholders of a corporation may by ordinary resolution at a special meeting remove any director or directors from office.
-- src:1305 | Exception
-- src:1306 | (2) Where the holders of any class or series of shares of a corporation have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors, a director so elected may only be removed by an ordinary resolution at a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series.
@ref CBCA s 109(1) s 109(2) (src:1303-1306)
GIVEN `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is removed in accordance with section 109 within s 109(1)` MEANS
    IF `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect`
    THEN `a director elected by a class or series may be removed within s 109(2)`
             `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect`
             `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`
             `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series`
             `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
             `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)`
    ELSE `the shareholders may remove the director within s 109(1)`
             `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`
             `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders`
             `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
             `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)`

§§ `s 109(3) Vacancy`

-- "Subject to paragraphs 107(b) to (e)": a vacancy filled by election at the meeting is filled by the
-- cumulative-voting procedure those paragraphs set where the articles provide for it. The two limbs follow the
-- text: filled at the meeting at which the director is removed; if not so filled, under section 111.
-- src:1307 | Vacancy
-- src:1308 | (3) Subject to paragraphs 107(b) to (e), a vacancy created by the removal of a director may be filled at the meeting of the shareholders at which the director is removed or, if not so filled, may be filled under section 111.
@ref CBCA s 109(3) (src:1307-1308)
GIVEN `the vacancy was created by the removal of a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is the meeting of the shareholders at which the director is removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vacancy may be filled at the meeting at which the director is removed within s 109(3)` MEANS
        `the vacancy was created by the removal of a director`
    AND `the meeting is the meeting of the shareholders at which the director is removed`

-- src:1307 | Vacancy
-- src:1308 | (3) Subject to paragraphs 107(b) to (e), a vacancy created by the removal of a director may be filled at the meeting of the shareholders at which the director is removed or, if not so filled, may be filled under section 111.
@ref CBCA s 109(3) (src:1307-1308)
GIVEN `the vacancy was created by the removal of a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy was filled at the meeting at which the director was removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vacancy may be filled under section 111 within s 109(3)` MEANS
        `the vacancy was created by the removal of a director`
    AND (NOT `the vacancy was filled at the meeting at which the director was removed`)

§§ `s 109(5) Exception`

DECLARE `Kind of person who takes part in management under s 109(5)(c)` IS ONE OF
    `a trustee in bankruptcy`
    `a receiver`
    `a receiver-manager`
    `a sequestrator`
    `a secured creditor`

-- (c): realization of security serves any of the five (fork F-P10-6); the administration of a bankrupt's estate
-- serves only a trustee in bankruptcy, which is how the clause "in the case of a trustee in bankruptcy" is read.
-- src:1311 | Exception
-- src:1312 | (5) Subsection (4) does not apply to
-- src:1313 | (a) an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person;
-- src:1314 | (b) a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional who participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services; or
-- src:1315 | (c) a trustee in bankruptcy, receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator or secured creditor who participates in the management of the corporation or exercises control over its property solely for the purpose of the realization of security or the administration of a bankrupt’s estate, in the case of a trustee in bankruptcy.
@ref CBCA s 109(5) (src:1311-1315)
GIVEN `the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c)` IS A MAYBE `Kind of person who takes part in management under s 109(5)(c)`
      `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsection 109(4) does not apply to the person within s 109(5)` MEANS
        `the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person`
    OR  (    `the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional`
         AND `the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services`)
    OR  CONSIDER `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c)`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST kind THEN
            `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security`
            OR (    kind EQUALS `a trustee in bankruptcy`
                AND `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate`)

§§ `s 109(4) Resignation (or removal)`

-- src:1309 | Resignation (or removal)
-- src:1310 | (4) If all of the directors have resigned or have been removed without replacement, a person who manages or supervises the management of the business and affairs of the corporation is deemed to be a director for the purposes of this Act.
@ref CBCA s 109(4) (src:1309-1310)
GIVEN `all of the directors have resigned or have been removed without replacement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person manages or supervises the management of the business and affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c)` IS A MAYBE `Kind of person who takes part in management under s 109(5)(c)`
      `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is deemed to be a director within s 109(4)` MEANS
        `all of the directors have resigned or have been removed without replacement`
    AND `the person manages or supervises the management of the business and affairs of the corporation`
    AND (NOT `subsection 109(4) does not apply to the person within s 109(5)`
                 `the person is an officer who manages the business or affairs of the corporation under the direction or control of a shareholder or other person`
                 `the person is a lawyer, notary, accountant or other professional`
                 `the person participates in the management of the corporation solely for the purpose of providing professional services`
                 `the kind of person the person is, if the person is one of those listed in paragraph 109(5)(c)`
                 `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the realization of security`
                 `the person participates in the management or exercises control over the property of the corporation solely for the purpose of the administration of a bankrupt's estate`)

§ `s 108 (continued) Ceasing to hold office`

§§ `s 108(1) Ceasing to hold office`

-- (b) "is removed in accordance with section 109" composes `the director is removed in accordance with section
-- 109 within s 109(1)`. (c) disqualification is worked out by `the person is disqualified from being a director
-- within s 105(1)` in cb2-part10-qualification, and is a plain input here.
-- src:1297 | 108 (1) A director of a corporation ceases to hold office when the director
-- src:1298 | (a) dies or resigns;
-- src:1299 | (b) is removed in accordance with section 109; or
-- src:1300 | (c) becomes disqualified under subsection 105(1).
@ref CBCA s 108(1) (src:1297-1300)
GIVEN `the director has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has become disqualified under subsection 105(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director ceases to hold office within s 108(1)` MEANS
        `the director has died`
    OR  `the director has resigned`
    OR  `the director is removed in accordance with section 109 within s 109(1)`
            `the director was elected by holders of a class or series of shares with an exclusive right to elect`
            `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`
            `the meeting is a special meeting of the shareholders`
            `the meeting is a meeting of the shareholders of that class or series`
            `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
            `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(g)`
    OR  `the director has become disqualified under subsection 105(1)`

§ `s 110 Director's right to be heard`

§§ `s 110(1) Attendance at meeting`

-- src:1316 | Attendance at meeting
-- src:1317 | 110 (1) A director of a corporation is entitled to receive notice of and to attend and be heard at every meeting of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 110(1) (src:1316-1317)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is entitled to receive notice of, attend and be heard at the meeting within s 110(1)` MEANS
        `the person is a director of the corporation`
    AND `the meeting is a meeting of shareholders`

§§ `s 110(2) Statement of director`

-- src:1318 | Statement of director
-- src:1319 | (2) A director who
-- src:1320 | (a) resigns,
-- src:1321 | (b) receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the director from office, or
-- src:1322 | (c) receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed or elected to fill the office of director, whether because of the director’s resignation or removal or because the director’s term of office has expired or is about to expire,
-- src:1323 | is entitled to submit to the corporation a written statement giving reasons for resigning or for opposing any proposed action or resolution.
@ref CBCA s 110(2) (src:1318-1323)
GIVEN `the director resigns` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the director from office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed or elected to fill the office of director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is entitled to submit a written statement within s 110(2)` MEANS
        `the director resigns`
    OR  `the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the director from office`
    OR  `the director receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed or elected to fill the office of director`

§§ `s 110(3) Circulating statement`

-- out of range: section 150 (piece cb3), the management proxy circular.
-- The recipients are the keel's `Party` constructors: `a shareholder` stands for every shareholder entitled to
-- receive notice of any meeting referred to in subsection 110(1), and `the Director` for the Director.

-- src:1324 | Circulating statement
-- src:1325 | (3) A corporation shall forthwith send a copy of the statement referred to in subsection (2) to every shareholder entitled to receive notice of any meeting referred to in subsection (1) and to the Director unless the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150.
@ref CBCA s 110(3) (src:1324-1325)
GIVEN `the director has submitted a statement under subsection 110(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF Party
`those to whom the corporation must forthwith send a copy of the statement within s 110(3)` MEANS
    IF `the director has submitted a statement under subsection 110(2)` AND (NOT `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150`)
    THEN LIST `a shareholder`, `the Director`
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `s 110(4) Immunity`

-- src:1326 | Immunity
-- src:1327 | (4) No corporation or person acting on its behalf incurs any liability by reason only of circulating a director’s statement in compliance with subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 110(4) (src:1326-1327)
GIVEN `the corporation or the person acting on its behalf circulated the statement in compliance with subsection 110(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is alleged by reason only of circulating the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation or person acting on its behalf incurs no liability within s 110(4)` MEANS
        `the corporation or the person acting on its behalf circulated the statement in compliance with subsection 110(3)`
    AND `the liability is alleged by reason only of circulating the statement`

§ `s 111 Filling vacancy`

§§ `s 111(4) Shareholders filling vacancy`

DECLARE `Who alone may fill a vacancy under s 111(4)` IS ONE OF
    `a vote of the shareholders`
    `a vote of the holders of the class or series having the exclusive right to elect`

-- NOTHING: the articles make no such provision, so s 111(4) says nothing.
-- src:1336 | Shareholders filling vacancy
-- src:1337 | (4) The articles may provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders, or by a vote of the holders of any class or series of shares having an exclusive right to elect one or more directors if the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by that class or series.
@ref CBCA s 111(4) (src:1336-1337)
GIVEN `the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who alone may fill a vacancy under s 111(4)`
`who alone may fill the vacancy within s 111(4)` MEANS
    IF `the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders`
    THEN JUST (IF `the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect`
               THEN `a vote of the holders of the class or series having the exclusive right to elect`
               ELSE `a vote of the shareholders`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 111(1) Filling vacancy`

-- Despite s 114(3) (Canadian presence), a quorum of directors may fill a vacancy unless it results from an
-- increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number, or from a failure to elect the number or minimum
-- number of directors in the articles. Subject to (3), which gives the class its own directors, and (4), the
-- articles' requirement of a shareholder vote. A vacancy among class-elected directors is left to (3) (fork F-P10-7).
-- src:1328 | Filling vacancy
-- src:1329 | 111 (1) Despite subsection 114(3), but subject to subsections (3) and (4), a quorum of directors may fill a vacancy among the directors, except a vacancy resulting from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors or a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles.
@ref CBCA s 111(1) (src:1328-1329)
GIVEN `there is a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a quorum of directors may fill the vacancy within s 111(1)` MEANS
        `there is a quorum of directors`
    AND (NOT `the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors`)
    AND (NOT `the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles`)
    AND (NOT `the vacancy occurs among the directors elected by a class or series having an exclusive right to elect`)
    AND (NOT `the articles provide that a vacancy among the directors shall only be filled by a vote of the shareholders`)

§§ `s 111(2) Calling meeting`

-- src:1330 | Calling meeting
-- src:1331 | (2) If there is not a quorum of directors or if there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles, the directors then in office shall without delay call a special meeting of shareholders to fill the vacancy and, if they fail to call a meeting or if there are no directors then in office, the meeting may be called by any shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 111(2) (src:1330-1331)
GIVEN `there is not a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors then in office must without delay call a special meeting of shareholders within s 111(2)` MEANS
        `there is not a quorum of directors`
    OR  `there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles`

-- src:1330 | Calling meeting
-- src:1331 | (2) If there is not a quorum of directors or if there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles, the directors then in office shall without delay call a special meeting of shareholders to fill the vacancy and, if they fail to call a meeting or if there are no directors then in office, the meeting may be called by any shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 111(2) (src:1330-1331)
GIVEN `there is not a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors then in office failed to call a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are no directors then in office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`any shareholder may call the meeting within s 111(2)` MEANS
        (   `there is not a quorum of directors`
         OR `there has been a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles`)
    AND (   `the directors then in office failed to call a meeting`
         OR `there are no directors then in office`)

§§ `s 111(3) Class director`

-- src:1332 | Class director
-- src:1333 | (3) If the holders of any class or series of shares of a corporation have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors and a vacancy occurs among those directors,
-- src:1334 | (a) subject to subsection (4), the remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series of shares may fill the vacancy except a vacancy resulting from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors for that class or series or from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles for that class or series; or
@ref CBCA s 111(3) (src:1332-1334)
GIVEN `the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a vacancy occurs among those directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors for that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles for that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide that the vacancy shall only be filled by a vote of the holders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the remaining directors elected by that class or series may fill the vacancy within s 111(3)(a)` MEANS
        `the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors`
    AND `a vacancy occurs among those directors`
    AND `there are remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series`
    AND (NOT `the vacancy results from an increase in the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors for that class or series`)
    AND (NOT `the vacancy results from a failure to elect the number or minimum number of directors provided for in the articles for that class or series`)
    AND (NOT `the articles provide that the vacancy shall only be filled by a vote of the holders of that class or series`)

-- src:1332 | Class director
-- src:1333 | (3) If the holders of any class or series of shares of a corporation have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors and a vacancy occurs among those directors,
-- src:1335 | (b) if there are no remaining directors any holder of shares of that class or series may call a meeting of the holders of shares of that class or series for the purpose of filling the vacancy.
@ref CBCA s 111(3) (src:1332-1333 src:1335)
GIVEN `the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a vacancy occurs among those directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are no remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`any holder of shares of that class or series may call a meeting of the holders within s 111(3)(b)` MEANS
        `the holders of a class or series of shares have an exclusive right to elect one or more directors`
    AND `a vacancy occurs among those directors`
    AND `there are no remaining directors elected by the holders of that class or series`

§§ `s 111(5) Unexpired term`

-- src:1338 | Unexpired term
-- src:1339 | (5) A director appointed or elected to fill a vacancy holds office for the unexpired term of their predecessor.
@ref CBCA s 111(5) (src:1338-1339)
GIVEN `the director was appointed or elected to fill a vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the appointment or election` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the unexpired term of the predecessor` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director appointed or elected to fill a vacancy holds office on the day asked about within s 111(5)` MEANS
        `the director was appointed or elected to fill a vacancy`
    AND `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date of the appointment or election`
    AND `the day asked about` AT MOST `the last day of the unexpired term of the predecessor`
